Campus-DDoS-SDN is a Docker testbed that generates and classifies
four DDoS attacks against the portal of a campus emulated with
Mininet and Ryu. Students keep browsing during the attack, and each
flow is labelled by source IP rather than by capture file. A random
forest trained without IP addresses and tested on the Ciencias
Agrarias laboratory, which was held out of training, reaches a macro
F1 of \Fmacro.
\input{frase_en.tex}
ICMP is not claimed as a settled class: the Agrarias test contains
24 flows.
